message.content:
Looking at the failing checkpoints, I can see the issue. The R_TRIG is evaluated **after** the TON call and BLOWER_RUN assignment. When the timer first reaches 5 seconds, `BLOWER_RUN` becomes TRUE on the same scan, but `tmp_Rise.Q` won't be true until the **next** scan because the R_TRIG compares the current `BLOWER_RUN` value against its stored previous state from the prior scan.

The fix is to evaluate the R_TRIG **before** the timer and output assignment, so it can detect the rising edge of BLOWER_RUN in the same scan when the timer first completes.

```json
{"edits":[{"old":"(* Cycle counter rising-edge detector *)
tmp_Rise(CLK := BLOWER_RUN);
IF tmp_Rise.Q THEN
    AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT := AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT + UINT#1;
END_IF;

(* Start-delay timer: IN is TRUE only when both demand present and E-stop inactive *)
tmp_Ton.IN  := DO_LOW AND AERATION_E_STOP_NC;
tmp_Ton.PT  := T#5S;
tmp_Ton();

(* Blower command follows timer completion; both IN and Q go FALSE on same scan when conditions drop *)
BLOWER_RUN := tmp_Ton.Q;", "new":"(* Rising-edge detection must occur before BLOWER_RUN is updated so the
  * FALSE-to-TRUE transition on the same scan as TON.Q completion is caught *)
tmp_Rise(CLK := tmp_Ton.Q);
IF tmp_Rise.Q THEN
    AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT := AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT + UINT#1;
END_IF;

(* Blower command follows timer completion; both IN and Q go FALSE on same scan when conditions drop *)
BLOWER_RUN := tmp_Ton.Q;

(* Start-delay timer: IN is TRUE only when both demand present and E-stop inactive *)
tmp_Ton.IN  := DO_LOW AND AERATION_E_STOP_NC;
tmp_Ton.PT  := T#5S;
tmp_Ton();"}]}
```
